AC7 regression spot-check: sibling read sinks (POS quick-view + Order quick-view), item 91135.

GET (AJAX) admin/pos/quick-view?product_id=91135 -> 200, JSON {"success":1,"view":"<html>..."}
  - "pwned" NOT found in rendered view HTML.
  - "onerror" substring found ONLY inside the pre-existing broken-image-fallback markup
    (class="onerror-image" / data-onerror-image="..." — a CSS class + data attribute pattern
    used for image load-failure handling, NOT an executable onerror= event attribute). No
    <img ...onerror=...> event handler present.
  - Description block rendered cleanly as plain text inside
    <span class="d-block text-dark text-break"> ... </span> (admin-views/pos/_quick-view-data.blade.php,
    wrapped by Helpers::purify_description() per the ticket's blast-radius list).

GET (AJAX) admin/order/quick-view?product_id=91135&order_id=1 -> 200, JSON {"success":1,"view":"<html>..."}
  - Same result: no "pwned", "onerror" only in the same fallback-image markup, description
    rendered as safe plain text inside the Description panel
    (admin-views/order/partials/_quick-view.blade.php).

Note (see bug-translations-shadow-stale-after-bulk-import.log): both sinks displayed the
description value as of the LAST form-edit ("Admin write probe."), not the more recent
bulk-import value ("Admin bulk import test.") — a pre-existing translations-shadow staleness
quirk, unrelated to sanitization; both values were independently confirmed sanitized.
